statement:
Let $S\to S'$ be a morphism of schemes in a fixed big fppf site. Under the localization functor $j:(\Sch/S)_{fppf}\to(\Sch/S')_{fppf}$, Construction A (Stacks, Stacks and localization) regards a stack $\mathcal X\to(\Sch/S)_{fppf}$ as the same category fibred over $(\Sch/S')_{fppf}$ by composing its structural functor with $j$, together with its canonical morphism to $(\Sch/S)_{fppf}$. Conversely, Construction B regards a stack $\mathcal X'$ over $S'$ equipped with a map $\mathcal X'\to(\Sch/S)_{fppf}$ over $S'$ as a stack over $S$. These are mutually inverse 2-functors.

Let $\Sch_{fppf}$ be a big fppf site.
Let $S \to S'$ be a morphism of this site.
The constructions A and B of
Stacks, Section \ref{stacks-section-localize}
above give isomorphisms of $2$-categories
$$
\left\{
\begin{matrix}
2\text{-category of algebraic}\\
\text{stacks }\mathcal{X}\text{ over }S
\end{matrix}
\right\}
\leftrightarrow
\left\{
\begin{matrix}
2\text{-category of pairs }(\mathcal{X}', f)\text{ consisting of an}\\
\text{algebraic stack }\mathcal{X}'\text{ over }S'\text{ and a morphism}\\
f : \mathcal{X}' \to (\Sch/S)_{fppf}\text{ of algebraic stacks over }S'
\end{matrix}
\right\}
$$

